4.2.3 Digital output board (DO_1)
 The Digital Output board has 8 output channels with the following characteristics:
 ▪ 0÷110 V + 30% range;
 ▪ maximum current of 1 A for each channel;
 ▪ Each output channel belongs to a separately insulated zone (powered by a distinct and insulated
 section of the hybrid power supply unit);
 ▪ isolation between field side and digital side by means of optocouplers (1500 Vdc).
 ▪ Diagnostic and protection functionality:
 o Short-circuit detection with channel power supply reset;
 o Detection of not connected outputs;
 o Reset of all output channels when the feeding voltage at the control logic fails.
 o LIFE signal generated by the CPU board: if the life is not present, all the output channels
 are in normal state.

4.2.4 Analog Output board (AO_1)
 The analogue output board has 2 output channels with following characteristics:
 ▪ Voltage output with range 0÷10 V;
 ▪ Isolation between field side and CPU side by means of optocouplers and insulated power supply;
 ▪ Diagnostic and protection functionality:
 o Output failure feedback control;
 o LIFE signal generated by the CPU board: if the life is not present, all the output channels are
 reset.

/// 5. Monitoring software
 A Faiveley Transport dedicated software tool, called WSPMon as generic name, allows
 o monitoring of WSP system input/output;
 o maintenance;
 o recording.

This software tool is mainly composed of :
 o A control panel menu showing all I/O states on a single screen. This panel is linked to a
 simulator menu allowing to force specific I/O configuration at vehicle stop (option);
 o A recorder menu that allows to trace and record internal and external system's variables;
 o An error menu that allows managing the faults in a dedicated screen.

